        {
          "id": 1909094,
          "username": "devmont-digital",
          "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/community.shopify.com/devmont-digital/{size}/301355_2.png",
          "created_at": "2026-10-08T07:15:32.656Z",
          "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"zeed17\" data-post=\"1\" data-topic=\"694201\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/z/e36b37/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> zeed17:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>For those who receive product CSV files from suppliers:</p>\n<p>What does your workflow look like before importing the products into Shopify?</p>\n<p>For example, do you usually:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Clean or reorganize the supplier CSV?</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Rename/map columns?</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Handle missing or inconsistent data?</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Use a spreadsheet, a custom script, or an app?</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>I’m particularly interested in hearing how you handle this <strong>in practice</strong>, especially when different suppliers provide files in different formats.</p>\n<p>Thanks!</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>In practice, I usually handle this through an import app. First, I match the supplier’s product name and SKU with the existing Shopify data, then map the required fields and upload the CSV.</p>\n<p>If the client provides the product data separately, I clean and organize it into a proper Excel/CSV format first, make sure the names, SKUs, variants, prices, images, and other required fields are consistent, and then upload it through the app. This works well when different suppliers provide files in different formats because I can standardize the data before importing.</p>",
