    "ai_summary": {
      "id": 1876554,
      "summarized_text": "Supplier product CSVs often need standardizing before Shopify import, especially when each supplier uses different columns or data conventions. One workflow is to clean the file in a spreadsheet, map fields such as names, SKUs, variants, prices, and images, then import through an app. A reusable master sheet with a separate column map for each supplier can make repeat imports faster.\n\nKey checks and practices raised include:\n- Keep supplier SKUs alongside internal SKUs for matching future price lists and purchase orders.\n- Separate new-product imports from updates, so cost or barcode changes do not overwrite carefully maintained descriptions or inventory.\n- Check for duplicate SKUs, missing barcodes, and implausible costs; preserve image-to-product row alignment and test a small sample before a full import.\n- Normalize handles and vendor names, sanitize supplier-provided HTML, and apply pricing rules in a staging step.\n\nImport apps, spreadsheets, and purpose-built utilities were all mentioned. The discussion offers practical approaches but does not settle on one best workflow; the right method depends on supplier formats and whether the task is adding products or updating existing listings.",
